<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Concurrency Sigils ~ the record

The concurrency sigils speak their standing at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/holo`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/hui`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lele`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/puka`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/hoolele`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/tick`>>: the grammar table registers each, and no runtime executes one. This record keeps the status lines they carried, verbatim, and the forecast the tick hook waited on.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/status-lines`>>

!! The status lines, as written

Each role line closed on ''async-first concurrency sprint pending'' (holo, hui, lele, puka).

* holo: ''Grammar only --- the cancelling-race execution runtime awaits the async-first sprint.''
* hui: ''Grammar only --- the await-all join runtime awaits the async-first sprint.''
* lele: ''Grammar only --- the fire-and-continue execution runtime awaits the async-first sprint.''
* puka: ''Grammar only --- the selecting-race execution runtime awaits the async-first sprint.''
* hoolele: ''Concurrency runtime pending (async-first sprint). Current tiddler registers grammar only.''
* nihomano-sigils, the family heading: ''Concurrency sigils (async cluster; sprint pending)''.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tick-forecast`>>

!! The tick hook's forecast

The tick role line read ''DEFERRED to UE6 ~2027'', and its head read ''\tick (Deferred)''. Its status, verbatim:

> ''Status: DEFERRED'' — full pono law spec and Hawaiian proper name await Visual Verse tick node confirmation (UE6 target ~2027). … Concurrency runtime (async-first sprint) comes first as a prerequisite. Grammar registration alone stands.

The nihomano-sigils list carried the same forecast: ''Hawaiian proper name deferred pending Visual Verse tick node shape (UE6 ~2027)''. The nalu meme read: ''The `\tick` sigil (when it lands) will live at the grammar layer — it will be a device lifecycle declaration that says "run this procedure every nalu."''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/hoolele-boundary`>>

!! The hoolele boundary's first naming

The hoolele use cases first named the boundary by classes the design anticipated; no class named `MemeSyncAdaptor` or `VmPool` stands in code, and the api meme names the wiki shore (`IslandAdaptor`) and the vessel's island pool (`VesselIslandPool`) in their places. Verbatim:

> * ''`LarTiddlerStore` CRDT flush'' — must complete even if the `MemeSyncAdaptor` is disposed; spawn the flush, hold the task handle in the store.
> * ''`VmPool` cross-VM coordination'' — work that spans wiki VM instances has no single containing scope; spawn the coordination task at pool level.
>
> The `MemeSyncAdaptor` boundary IS the `hoolele` boundary in the Lararium stack: work above it (wiki reactions, widget handlers) uses structured concurrency; work below it (CRDT, network) uses `hoolele`-style spawn semantics in TS.

<<~/ahu>>

